      "@type": "Dataset",
      "name": "The Flat Rate Movers — Industrial Offices Move Operations Dataset",
      "description": "Industrial offices move operations from The Flat Rate Movers: office moves for industrial and facility sites — the office areas within plants, warehouses and industrial facilities — run on a planned, sequenced schedule so the site is working again on day one. The published process chain is: survey; phased plan; pack and label; sequenced move; install and place; verify; close-out. Scope moved: office furniture and equipment, files and fixtures, with the packing, protection and placement that goes with them. The move is planned around production and site access, not around an hourly meter, and is quoted at one flat rate agreed in writing before move day. Where an office-area item is high-mass (1,500 to 3,500 lbs), it moves under SIR Structural Integrity Relocation and the KIM-GS Protocol with L/360 floor-deflection analysis before anything is lifted. Where the same job also needs warehouse or project-support teams, it connects to Industrial & Commercial Services, priced per job with no required contract duration.",
